Subject: Rules download at start-up; a card's second face is labelled

Right after a restart the rules tools answered from the bundled
Comprehensive Rules copy until the first rules call started the download
of the current one, so answers a minute apart named two effective dates.
The download now starts when the server starts (MYSTIC_FORGE_NO_CR_WARMUP
switches it off; the tests set it).

A two-face card in a search result was printed with a bare "---" between
its faces, the marker the numbered list puts between results, so a reader
took the second face for another card. The second face is now headed
"Other face of <card name>:".

